{"kind": "report", "step": 17, "ts": "2026-11-19T14:21:13.588053+00:00", "data": {"category": "wan", "host": "external", "component": "provider_network", "cause": "The provider's network stopped carrying our traffic: the modem lost ranging (T3 timeout) at 02:01:44, failed re-registration (\"TFTP failed - configuration file NOT FOUND\"), then rebooted and reported \"registration complete\" at 02:28:21 \u2014 yet the ISP gateway 198.51.100.1 still does not pass any traffic even after two WAN reloads by the watchdog.", "evidence": ["Modem log /var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-events.jsonl: 02:01:44 'No Ranging Response received - T3 time-out'; 02:14:10 'TFTP failed - configuration file NOT FOUND'; 02:28:21 'Cable Modem Reboot because of - unknown; registration complete' \u2014 outage began ~02:01 matching the ranging loss.", "ping -c 3 -n 198.51.100.1 on gw.lan: 100% packet loss to the ISP-side gateway, while arp -n shows a live ARP entry for 198.51.100.1 (00:17:10:9a:a3:96), so the link is up to layer 2 but no traffic passes beyond it.", "ifconfig vtnet0: WAN UP/RUNNING/LOWER_UP with lease address 198.51.100.27; netstat -rn shows default via 198.51.100.1; /var/db/dhclient.leases.vtnet0 shows a valid lease (expires 2026/3/6), so addressing is not the problem.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/state.json: reloads_in_outage=2, last_action=reload; events.jsonl shows reload decisions at 02:30 and a retry at 02:40 after the modem became OPERATIONAL \u2014 WAN renewals did not restore connectivity.", "modem-metrics.jsonl: cm_status OPERATIONAL from 02:29 onward with good SNR (min_snr 37.6-37.9 dB), so the modem itself is synced and registered; only downstream forwarding fails.", "ping -c 3 -n 10.20.0.9 (LAN host) succeeds, confirming local services/network are fine."], "action": "contact_provider", "recommendation": "Contact the ISP: report that the cable connection lost ranging at 02:01:44 with a subsequent provisioning failure (\"TFTP failed - configuration file NOT FOUND\") and that although the modem now reports registration complete, the ISP-side gateway passes no traffic. Ask them to check the CMTS/provisioning side for this circuit. A further WAN reload or modem reboot is unlikely to help \u2014 two lease renewals already ran during the outage without effect, and the modem already re-registered on its own.", "detail": "ISP side of the WAN link not passing traffic despite modem registration", "fix": "none", "contributing": {"host": "gw.lan", "component": "wan_dhcp_lease"}}}
